skill: "corporate-governance-resolutions"
sections[3]:
  - "# corporate-governance-resolutions\n\nDraft board and shareholder resolutions from precedent, verify them against bylaws and jurisdiction requirements, and keep the corporate records index current. Use when a corporate action needs approval (grants, financings, officer appointments, policy adoptions), before a board meeting, or when an auditor or bank asks for evidence of authority.\n\nOwner: role-general-counsel (pod-gna, legal). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"corporate action request (type, parties, amounts); bylaws and charter; prior resolutions registry resolutions-registry.toon; board calendar and approval workflow\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/legal/resolution-draft.toon with recitals, operative clauses, certification block; resolutions-registry.toon update; records index entry\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Identify the corporate action type and the approving body required for it (board, shareholders, committee) from bylaws and charter; the body is determined by the documents, not by convenience.\n2. Pull the closest prior resolutions from resolutions-registry.toon; precedent is cited per clause, and departures from precedent are stated as departures.\n3. Draft recitals (the facts that make the action proper) and operative clauses (what is approved, in what amount, with what authority and conditions).\n4. Verify against jurisdiction requirements with search_web where the requirement is external (filings, witnesses, notarization); label anything unverifiable as requiring outside-counsel confirmation.\n5. Check consistency with existing instruments: an approval that conflicts with an investor agreement covenant is flagged, not drafted around.\n6. Assemble the certification block: who certifies, what is attached, and the scope of reliance for third parties relying on the resolution.\n7. Emit ask_question to the operator for board workflow (agenda placement, vote mechanics); the counsel role does not convene the board itself.\n8. On approval, file the signed resolution in the registry, update resolutions-registry.toon and the records index with references; the registry is what banks and auditors rely on.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nsigned resolutions to registry; authority evidence to finance and audit on request.\n"
